A||N||19||87ECO5||Things to see while in Toney, Alabama||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||02-12-2001||02:06 PM||||I'm heading down this Friday to hand my 4-cylinder car over to the man himself.  In 1-2 weeks, he'll give it back to me with two additional cylinders!<P>Question - besides The Fiero Factory, what else is worth visiting while down in Northern Alabama?||||reg||5
Z||000001||DRH||02-12-2001||02:18 PM||||Space and rocket center (NASA) is just a few miles down the road outside of Huntsville. I haven't been there in years, but they used to have a museum with some pretty cool stuff if you're into that sort of thing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECO5||02-12-2001||03:12 PM||||Anyone in the area interested in getting together Saturday morning, the 17th, for breakfast or something?  I'd love to meet more people from the forum!<P>We'll be staying at a hotel outside of Huntsville and probably won't be leaving for home until 10:00 or so.||||reg||5
Z||000003||1FST2M6||02-12-2001||03:34 PM||||Lake Guntersville. and go fishing...  uum in Chattanooga, Lookout MTN.. Ruby Falls, Rock City... thats all on the way to and Fro.. and the Tennessee aquarium.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||02-12-2001||08:24 PM||||In Huntsville: Space and Rocket Center, Intergraph (If you're into that.)<P>Fairly close: Little River Canyon ( <A HREF="http://www.nps.gov/liri/index.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nps.gov/liri/index.htm</A> )<BR><p>[This message has been edited by MrPBody (edited 02-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||PAUL88GT||02-14-2001||07:13 PM||||87EC05:<P>Not much to see in Toney other than the Fiero Factory, but there are lots of fun things to do and see in the Huntsville area.  The link below covers most of them:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.huntsville.org/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.huntsville.org/</A> <P>The ones that I encourage visitors to see are<BR>1) Space and Rocket Center including tour of the NASA Marshall Space Flight Center (takes at least half a day)<BR>2) Jack Daniels Distillery in Lynchburg Tennessee (about 40-50) miles from The Fiero Factory. Great tour even if you don't consume their product. A historic landmark. Tour is free and takes a couple of hours. No, they don't provide samples. It's a dry county (no alcohol sold). The little town square is kinda neat.<P>Unfortunately, I am not available Saturday morning because of family committments, but I can possibly meet you on the return trip. Send me an e-mail before you return.<P>Have a safe trip.<BR>Paul<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Wolfhound||02-15-2001||07:15 AM||||Be sure to visit the Space and Rocket Center.<BR>They have an SR-71 spy plane , a standing Saturn 5, I-MAX movie for starters. you can easily spend a day there.<BR> You will see more fieros on the road in Huntsville than probably any other city. May be due to the Fiero Factory being near by.<BR> ||||reg||14
Z||000007||bHooper||02-15-2001||09:39 AM||||Scott,  thanks for starting this thread!  It seems my fiance' and I will be going to Toney, Al for our honeymoon   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Wonder what we will be doing?<P>hehehehe<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000008||87ECO5||02-15-2001||10:50 AM||||<B>PAUL88GT</B> - thanks for the kind wishes.  Now looks like I won't be getting it back until the swap meet in April.  Are you planning to attend that?<P><B>bHooper</B> - glad I could help, Brian!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   When are you going?<P><B>everyone</B> - thanks for the information.<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 02-15-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000009||bHooper||02-15-2001||01:43 PM||||as we have now decided to "allope" (basically get married here, but not invite anyone, or spend any money), we will be travelling the country for about 2 weeks, after that.  the best thing was, that she even said it would be nice to stop by and see Ed and Rosie!  Damn, am I a lucky man or what?!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000010||PAUL88GT||02-15-2001||03:03 PM||||87:<BR>I will definitely attend the swap meet. I look forward to meeting you and other forum members there. I attended last year also.<P>bhooper:<BR>Congrats on your wedding. I can think of more exiting places than Toney to have a honeymoon. One thing for sure. You will have peace and quiet there.<P>Huntsville is good place to work and raise a family. One thing it is not is a party town. Not much night life to choose from. Probably a few more Fieros than normal thanks to Ed. <BR>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000011||PAUL88GT||02-21-2001||02:12 PM||||87EC05:<BR>I was at the Fiero Factory this past Monday. Which car was yours? I saw a white coupe and and a Burgundy GT with Ohio plates. Also saw a new 3.4 engine on a hoist. Ed was picking up a car so I did not get to see him.<BR>Paul ||||reg||1
